Here is how to create assert statements:

```csharp
    // For Add() method, New_Ret value should be 0 because it is not added yet.
    Debug.Assert(New_Ret == Old_arrListCount, $"Add() method failed for arrListCount: {Old_arrListCount}");
```

The "Debug.Assert" is used to debug the application. The first parameter of the "Assert" statement decides if it is executed or not (if the statement is false) and the second parameter is a message that will be shown if the Assert executes. It is similar to the throw statement available in C#.

Note that, this "Debug.Assert" works in Debug mode only and throws runtime exception when the Assert is executed. 

