It seems to be a code generated by an automated test framework Pex. In the code provided, each method contains a comment starting with "@@@". Those comments are not standard comments, but custom comments defined by the Pex test framework. 

When Pex runs, it parses this code to generate new test cases. While inspecting the properties of this code, it can recognize custom annotations and perform certain actions.

The comment you mentioned "@@@ If the return value is true, index of x in old array is greater than or equal to that in new array" is not valid in C#. The code should be corrected to a proper C# or other recognized language syntax or the comment should be defined in Pex to be more meaningful. 

